'''''{{PAGENAME}}''''' is the upcoming fifty-first season of the CBS competitive reality television series ''{{dab|Survivor|U.S.}}''.

==Production==
During the {{S2|50}} [[Reunion (In the Hands of the Fans)|live reunion]], host [[Jeff Probst]] explained that the season would heavily incorporate past game mechanics, [[Hidden Immunity Idol]]s, and other [[Advantage|advantages]] to keep castaways on their toes. He branded the season as the beginning of the "Open Era" of ''Survivor''. Probst teased:

{{quote|prod|The "Open Era" is that anything “that has ever happened at any time on the show can happen in any season at any time in any order without any warning.<ref>https://variety.com/2026/tv/news/survivor-season-50-winner-51-the-open-era-1236755662/</ref>|Jeff Probst}}

While the show will continue identifying seasons by number, Probst stated that the producers would reconsider using themed seasons again in the future.<ref>https://people.com/survivor-season-51-everything-to-know-11979442</ref>

==Twists/Changes==
*'''26-Day Game'''
*'''Tribe Division:''' The castaways were divided into 2 tribes. No unifying theme was used in dividing the tribes.
*'''Returning Game Mechanics:''' Throughout the season, multiple game mechanics, idols, and advantages from previous seasons were heavily incorporated.
*'''[[Shot in the Dark]]'''

